{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095234-advice-on-a-nephandic-cult","id":1095234,"title":"Advice on a Nephandic cult,","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T14:02:13-07:00","id":1095234,"title":"Advice on a Nephandic cult,","content":"I came up with a Nephandic cult and I need advice on it. The basic concept is that they are a fraternal order of sailors called The Brothers of Oceanus. Their members are consisted of sailors, commercial fishermen and other people who make their living on the ocean. The Brothers seem to be a mostly innocent gathering of sea dogs that meet every month to discuss their jobs and their lifestyles while on the ocean. But mysteriously, everywhere the Brothers establish Lodges, water based deaths seem to escalate. Some victims are found floating in harbor's while others are found drowned in their bathtub.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe people behind these murders are the Brothers. They do this for their masters, a group of Nephandi. The Nephandi who founded the brothers are servants of the Outer Lords. How the sailors fell under their influence is unknown, but the Brothers seem to be extremely loyal to their masters.<br /> <br /> \u200bI need help detailing this cult's methods and detailing how they stay under the radar of the Technocrats and Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":".  Grammer mistakes 05-21-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:55:27-07:00","id":1095292,"title":"","content":"Am I right in thinking the brothers themselves aren't actually awakened, they are just part of the exclusive club and believe their nephandic masters words?<br /> <br /> If so, I'd say staying out of the Technocracys radar would be fairly easy. They sail all over the place so they can commit their crimes all over the world without causing too much suspicion, shipping off long before the investigators even learn of the missing personnel.<br /> <br /> One month you're in Mumbai, the next you're in Bangkok. Who's going to notice a few sailors by a dockyard? Who's going to tell one apart from another? And who's going to care what a bunch of sleepers are doing anyway? These places are where crime is common. As far as the NWO is concerned, crime is necessary to keep the masses fearful enough to demand more security in exchange for giving up control to them, while the Syndicate actively encourage criminal activity within their circles &quot;don't call it crime, call it... playing the game with alternative rules&quot; so they probably wouldn't be all that interested in a few nondescript murders, especially ones that happen all over the world and seem so unconnected.<br /> <br /> As for the methods, perhaps they coordinate the killings to be geometrically significant with the patterns of the stars and planets, or maybe they are making sacrifices to the deep ones that live far beneath the ocean floor (which is the same thing as space if you go deep enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T20:12:34-07:00","id":1095339,"title":"","content":"Maybe the sailors and fishermen are doing it all for a very ancient reason: sacrifices, in return for fair weather and plentiful catches.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi at the head of the cult are experts in Entropy, Forces, and Life. They grant their followers good fortune, manipulate the weather to ensure safe travel, and make the sea more bountiful. Humans have sacrificed prodigiously - even human lives - for much the same, since time immemorial. Certain types of fishermen would especially enjoy these services; Deadliest Catch isn't a popular documentary for nothing. Crab fishing can be a brutal occupation. Some of those who tackle the profession would love an edge, both to protect their lives and to ensure maximum profit margins. Let someone else pay the human cost for the public's supply of crab, for a change.<br /> <br /> Hell, the cult doesn't even need to be Nephandic. It just has to have mages at their head that venerate ancient gods, and engage in brutal rites. The sea is a harsh mistress, and demands blood to be placated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the cult could be getting material rewards directly. In exchange for sacrifices, the members receive gold, jewels, and perhaps some unearthly power. Read <i>The Shadow Over Innsmouth</i>, and note the deal the fish men have with the titular port town. Some high-ranking members could be Infernalists that obtained Investments, that make them look like creepy fish people (but, on the other hand, make them more long-lived and powerful).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T20:53:36-07:00","id":1095344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095234-advice-on-a-nephandic-cult?p=1095339#post1095339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the sailors and fishermen are doing it all for a very ancient reason: sacrifices, in return for fair weather and plentiful catches.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi at the head of the cult are experts in Entropy, Forces, and Life. They grant their followers good fortune, manipulate the weather to ensure safe travel, and make the sea more bountiful. Humans have sacrificed prodigiously - even human lives - for much the same, since time immemorial. Certain types of fishermen would especially enjoy these services; Deadliest Catch isn't a popular documentary for nothing. Crab fishing can be a brutal occupation. Some of those who tackle the profession would love an edge, both to protect their lives and to ensure maximum profit margins. Let someone else pay the human cost for the public's supply of crab, for a change.<br /> <br /> Hell, the cult doesn't even need to be Nephandic. It just has to have mages at their head that venerate ancient gods, and engage in brutal rites. The sea is a harsh mistress, and demands blood to be placated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the cult could be getting material rewards directly. In exchange for sacrifices, the members receive gold, jewels, and perhaps some unearthly power. Read <i>The Shadow Over Innsmouth</i>, and note the deal the fish men have with the titular port town. Some high-ranking members could be Infernalists that obtained Investments, that make them look like creepy fish people (but, on the other hand, make them more long-lived and powerful).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can rework the Nephandi into two corrupt Dreamspeakers, a brother and sister, who lead the cult and have them worship a obscure ocean deity from the South Pacific. The deity, according to the siblings, demanded human sacrifices. Instead of risking getting caught due to highly ritualized killings, the Brothers decided to make sacrifices to this Deity by drowning people while chanting the sacrificial prayer. After the ritual, the cultists try their hardest to make the drownings look like accidents. Luckily for them, they usually get shipped off to different ports of call because of their jobs and don't get to stick around for the police investigation. Apparently, something in the Umbra is accepting these sacrifices because fishermen who are members seem to be getting bigger hauls while sailors seem to be stumbling upon valuables floating on the ocean while on their voyages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}